<ArticleLayout slug="automotive-content-without-shipping-a-car" ctaLabel="Brief a vehicle launch" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">You can launch a vehicle in fifteen markets without putting it on a ship. What you cannot do is leave the motoring rules behind. Regulators judge the driving in the picture, however the picture was made.</p>

  <h2>Can car advertising use CGI with no photoshoot?</h2>

  <p>Yes. No advertising code or ruling read for this piece bars a generated or CGI car ad. The UK regulator has judged a fully computer-generated car poster under its ordinary rules and upheld the complaint against it. hubStudio generates environments around a vehicle, and the driving shown still has to pass the same tests as film.</p>

  <p>This page describes production practice, not legal advice. The codes and rulings are cited so your compliance team can read them at source. Reviewed September 24, 2026.</p>

  <p>Start with the asset list, because the answer changes line by line.</p>

